1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,433
Ima, he's the reason
why I lost my job!

2
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:04,533
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:05,700
[IMA] It was you?

4
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,733
You bastard! You're the reason
my daughter is worn out!

5
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:13,433
Are you sure
she's related to Don Nato?

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,500
Maybe you can check it again.

7
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,600
She scammed me once.

8
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:19,367
- Me?
- Right?

9
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:22,600
You used my<i> tocino</i> (cured pork)
for a free promo.

10
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:24,033
[SCOFFS]

11
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:26,233
"His tocino."

12
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,767
Hey.

13
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:29,500
You really are shameless.

14
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:31,533
You had the nerve
to say "my tocino".

15
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:33,400
Do you even own
that<i> tocino</i> brand?

16
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,433
You own...

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,500
Pindang Tocino?

18
00:00:51,633 --> 00:00:53,033
Will they be living here?

19
00:00:53,267 --> 00:00:54,267
[ZIA] Of course.

20
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:55,700
Once you get married.

21
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:57,233
- No!
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

22
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,533
I'm not going to
marry a scammer.

23
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:00,567
Hey, watch it!

24
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,600
You're so full of yourself!

25
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,733
Don't marry that man.

26
00:01:04,467 --> 00:01:05,633
Who does he think he is?

27
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:07,200
[JUNE] You think you're cute?

28
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:13,300
[JUNE]<i> Will I be living
</i> in a house full of pork now?

29
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,433
<i>Is it 'Bye sparkling lights
of the city</i>

30
00:01:16,433 --> 00:01:18,300
<i>and back to lonely dark nights'?</i>

31
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:20,500
You have to convince Ping, June.

32
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,800
Because if Don Nato's will
falls through,

33
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,733
all his estate and assets
will go to his foundation.

34
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,033
Dear, you know what,

35
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:31,567
you don't have to do this.
Let's go home.

36
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,300
We can always earn that money.

37
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,333
We're hardworking, remember?

38
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:36,700
Don't do this. Come on.

39
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:37,900
Ima.

40
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:41,067
No matter how much hard work
we put into day and night,

41
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,400
I don't think
we can ever afford a house.

42
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,733
This is a sure win.

43
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,133
Game, Attorney.

44
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:49,067
We'll stay here.

45
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:52,767
I'll make sure
Papa Ping falls in love with me.

46
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,567
[IMA] Hold up.

47
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,367
I didn't like the sound of that.

48
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,700
Men should be the ones
courting the women.

49
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,367
[JUNE] Ima!

50
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:02,767
It's different now.
All genders are equal.

51
00:02:02,767 --> 00:02:03,767
And besides...

52
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:06,100
Miss Judith is coming.

53
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,167
[SILLY SFX PLAYING]

54
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,600
[WHISPERS] Judith who?

55
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,433
[WHISPERS]
<i> Judith, due date. The bills.</i>

56
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:13,167
We have to do
what's best right now.

57
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,700
Alright.

58
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:17,167
[JUNE] Wait up!

59
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:20,133
[BODY THUDS]

60
00:02:20,133 --> 00:02:22,200
I'll not get down
until you get out of this car!

61
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,167
I might throw up
but I'll keep fighting!

62
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,800
[TAPS LOUDLY] Get out!

63
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:34,333
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]
